This is a bug in `es-module-lexer`, not in Vite itself [3]. The dev server's import analysis misparses a class method literally named `import(...)` (e.g. TensorFlow.js's HashTable `import(keys, values)` pulled in via `@aws-amplify/ui-react-liveness` [5]), producing `SyntaxError: Unexpected token '('`. The fix was reverted in #22827, so the issue was reopened [1]. A user-supplied workaround is a custom Vite plugin that rewrites the corrupted `import(` call in the response body [2][4]:

```ts
// vite.config.ts
export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [fixDevExpressImportMethodFalsePositive()],
});
```

The excerpts don't include the full plugin source, so the complete workaround code isn't available here.

This is a known bug in Vite 8's dev pre-bundler: `import Foo from "cjs-package"` resolves to the whole CJS exports wrapper object `{ default: Component, ... }` instead of the unwrapped `exports.default`, while `vite build` works correctly [4]. The pre-bundled output ends with `export default require_lib();`, which returns the entire exports object rather than unwrapping `.default` [4]. It was closed in #22232 [1], and bluwy noted it's probably related to the "consistent CommonJS interop" migration guide [3]. The reporter observed that the documented behavior—that `module.exports.__esModule` is not set to `true`—wasn't being honored [5].

Workarounds from the report [4]:

```ts
// For packages with a named export (e.g. react-qr-code):
import { QRCode } from "react-qr-code";

// For packages with only exports.default (e.g. react-simple-code-editor):
// use a runtime fallback
```

This is a known compatibility issue: after upgrading Vite to `7.3.2`, `@vitejs/plugin-legacy` fails during the legacy downgrade/transformation flow, and the failure appears with `esbuild@0.27.7` and later [4][3]. A maintainer identified it as an upstream esbuild issue, https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4436 [5], and the issue is labeled `bug: upstream` with a `has workaround` label [1].

The workaround is to pin esbuild back to `0.27.4` via an override [4]:

```json
{
  "overrides": {
    "esbuild": "0.27.4"
  }
}
```

After reinstalling dependencies, the problem disappears [4]. The expectation is that the fix will come from upstream esbuild rather than a Vite version rollback [2].

This is a `@googlemaps/js-api-loader` issue, not a Vite bug — it must be fixed on the loader side or worked around by the user [1]. Two workarounds reported in the thread:

1. Set `ssr.noExternal: ['@googlemaps/js-api-loader']` in `vite.config.ts`, keeping the normal named import [2]:
```ts
import { Loader } from '@googlemaps/js-api-loader';
```
2. Import the namespace and destructure (reported to work in dev, build, SSR, and prerendering) [4]:
```ts
import * as gmapsLoader from '@googlemaps/js-api-loader';
const { Loader } = gmapsLoader;
```

The reported error is a Vite dependency-optimizer issue with `moment` [1]. The workaround that users confirmed works is to alias `moment` to its CommonJS entry file in `vite.config.js` [3][5]:

```js
// vite.config.js
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import vue from '@vitejs/plugin-vue';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [vue()],
  resolve: {
    alias: {
      'moment': 'moment/moment.js'
    }
  }
});
```

An alternative alias form using `find`/`replacement` with `resolve('./node_modules/moment/moment.js')` was also suggested [1]. A contributor noted the code seems to need `moment.default.isMoment` to get `isMoment` [4].

这是 Vite 库模式下的已知问题（#8412），目前尚未完全修复 [1]。有贡献者指出，问题的关键其实不是 `rollupOptions.output.banner` 本身，而是 `\n` [2]。

在修复前，可以用一个 `enforce: 'post'` 的插件在 `generateBundle` 中手动给 chunk 加上 banner/footer 来绕过 [3]：

```ts
const bannerPlugin = {
  name: 'banner',
  enforce: 'post',
  generateBundle(options, bundle) {
    const banner = '/*! banner  */'
    const footer = ''
    for (const module of Object.values(bundle)) {
      if (module.type === 'chunk') {
        module.code = banner + module.code + footer
        // should change source map if needed
      }
    }
  }
}
```

如果想继续在 `vite.config.js` 里使用 `build.rollupOptions.output.banner/.footer`，可以改用读取 `options.banner()` / `options.footer()` 的插件版本 [4]；若产物带 shebang，还需保留首行 shebang 再插入 banner [5]。
